@ [governing_goal] continue dependency-safe local Cantor work throughout the active five-hour shift without live-provider hidden-state persistence or external-effect operations

& [PreservedUserDirection]
  + "start another 5-hour turn"
  + when a current job requires more attention than the frame provides hash the current frame and create a re-entry to take the next step
  + compiled attention procedures should reduce repeated attention material to inputs outputs conditions and transforms while retaining a hardened pattern handle
  + Honesty and Security should guard identity and trust boundaries before other patterns load

& [InheritedIntention]
  + Slice6B binds a compact frame to exact retained prefix custody
  + Slice6C distinguishes canonical full replay from the request selected for experimental model-facing transport
  + the transport packet itself still needs a small inspectable integrity surface so corruption can be detected before canonical custody is consulted
  + self-integrity must never be represented as provenance signature semantic truth provider admission or proof that omitted history is available

& [SelectedImplementationClaim]
  + activate a provider-free strict AttentionTransportEnvelope over one Slice6C transport
  + bind profile phase transport kind optional iteration index actual request SHA-256 request digest optional exact AttentionReentryFrame optional frame SHA-256 digest optional retained-prefix digest local-integrity-only flag and fixed nonclaims
  + full-prefix first transport has Advance phase iteration zero and no reentry frame frame digest or retained-prefix digest
  + compact iteration transports have Advance phase their canonical iteration index and an exact frame frame digest and retained-prefix digest echo
  + compact terminal reflection has ReflectTerminal phase no iteration index and an exact frame frame digest and retained-prefix digest echo
  + digest canonical compact JSON bytes of the request and frame with an explicit domain tag so identities cannot be interchanged
  + local validation recomputes only self-contained digests shape and claim fields
  + canonical validation first validates the complete Slice6C projection then recompiles the exact envelope from the selected canonical transport and requires equality
  + project a ScriptedTransportEnvelopeSet for every iteration transport and terminal reflection transport in exact order

& [Acceptance]
  + deterministic fixture yields one envelope per canonical iteration plus one terminal envelope
  + every envelope passes local validation without access to canonical history
  + every envelope passes stronger validation against its exact Slice6C transport and canonical custody
  + local validation rejects request bytes frame bytes digest algorithm digest value phase kind index retained-prefix echo flag nonclaim and unknown-field mutations
  + canonical validation rejects locally coherent substitution reordering cross-record and terminal-versus-iteration envelope changes
  + normalized strict JSON round trip and repeated fixture generation are deterministic

& [IdentityBoundary]
  + request_digest means integrity of the request bytes carried by this envelope
  + frame_digest means integrity of the frame bytes carried by this envelope
  + retained_prefix_digest remains the frame's commitment to host-custodied history and cannot reconstruct that history
  + local_integrity_only must remain true because self-consistency is weaker than canonical replay binding
  + canonical validation is a reconstruction comparison performed by the host and does not turn the envelope into a digital signature

& [Rollback]
  + P0 through Slice6C and all canonical and compact request forms remain unchanged
  + removing the isolated transport_envelope module exports and tests removes Slice6D without data migration

& [Boundary]
  + no key management digital signature producer authentication trust policy semantic truth provider model process HTTP socket tokenizer timing persistence concurrency remote EVO-X2 OneDrive hidden state KV cache live token effect FPGA or Minecraft activation
